; partypage.eval - a party built on the CREATION PAGE starts the game it shows
; (docs/party-creation-plan.md, phase 3).
;
; Run ON ITS OWN, first thing:  Dungeon.exe -headless -eval <this file>
; The page lives on the title screen, and `partypage open` refuses anywhere
; else - so this cannot follow a suite that has already started a game. Run it
; on the DEBUG build: the language step below is a use-after-free check, and
; the debug heap is what turns that into a crash.
;
; Every line is one of the page's own edits (the methods its widgets call), so
; this is the page's code path, not a second one. `partypage shows <member>
; <name>` is the one CHECK: it refuses - and the run then exits 1 - unless
; PartyCreationPage::ShownName gives that member that name (`-` = none, which
; the slot draws as "New member"). ShownName is the one rule the slot draws its
; name from (and the name field and Start read), so this checks the RULE, not
; the drawn slot: a slot that went back to its own copy of the rule would pass
; here, and a headless run never draws anyway. What it should show:
;   - the page opens on one new member, refusing to start ("needs a name");
;   - Kira, an elf: STR 9 DEX 14 VIT 8 WIL 10 INT 11 after DEX +2 (the elf's
;     DEX +2 INT +1 / VIT -2 STR -1 on 10), Blades and Throwing at level 2, a
;     dagger in hand and a rock in the pack;
;   - the LANGUAGE changes with the page open and the page still edits and reads
;     (code-review C370: its tree was cleared and not rebuilt, and the next
;     frame's text went into freed widgets - a crash in debug);
;   - Default party replaces her with the four; Brand's name field cleared still
;     shows Brand, as the game would start him (C109: the slot's own copy read
;     "New member"); Brand turned orc becomes a made member (STR 13 VIT 11 INT 8
;     WIL 8) with no kit, still Brand; two removed;
;   - Start: `roster` prints exactly the three the page last showed, and the
;     game is playing.
; A scripted `lang` is drawn but never saved (Game::m_scriptLanguage), so a run
; that dies between `lang de` and `lang en` leaves settings.ini as it was; the
; `lang en` only puts the rest of this run back in English.

logecho on
state
partypage open
partypage
partypage shows 0 -

partypage set name=Kira race=elf portrait=portrait135
partypage spend dex 2
partypage skill 0 blade
partypage skill 1 throwing
partypage item 0 dagger
partypage item 1 rock
partypage
partypage shows 0 Kira

lang de
partypage
partypage spend wil 1
partypage spend wil -1
partypage shows 0 Kira
lang en
partypage

partypage default
partypage set name=
partypage shows 0 Brand
partypage set race=orc
partypage shows 0 Brand
partypage select 3
partypage set name=Old_Tilo
partypage shows 3 Old_Tilo
partypage remove 1
partypage remove 1
partypage add
partypage shows 2 -
partypage set name=Kira race=elf portrait=portrait135
partypage spend dex 2
partypage skill 0 blade
partypage item 0 dagger
partypage

partypage start
roster
state
